hi  so i remember from last lockdown that my  focus was completely shot out of the  roof when lockdown was happening where i  live and now lockdown is happening again  and i already noticed that the last two  weeks i had such trouble focusing so if  you recognize yourself in this  i will give some tips and tricks during  this video of what i have learned the  last week on trying to increase my focus  and productivity  and yeah i hope you learned something so  hi i'm charlotte fraser a phd student in  computational neuroscience in the donors  institute in the netherlands  and this month i want to spend a little  bit on  establishing some healthy habits or  routines that can help me get through  the what is it fourth lockdown i'm not  entirely sure anymore what is time what  is memories  anyways so i want to establish some  healthy habits and routines that can  help me stay focused on my phd and  hopefully stay a little bit productive  so this week i have three things i  really wanted to focus on the first was  deep work the second was establishing  some healthy habits for my body and my  mind and the last one was a little bit  about mindset  so the first thing i focused on was deep  work and that's based on the book by cal  newport called deep work and he really  establishes this difference between deep  work on the one hand and shallow work on  the other hand so deep work in your phd  or during your studies could be  writing up your big projects doing the  coding doing the really important  basic things for your project and  shallow work on the other hand is then  reading emails for example or going to  all these meetings or random lectures  about productivity which i go to a lot  but anyways let's ignore that  so i wanted to establish this week a  little bit more focus on  deep work and call newport gives several  tricks and little habits that you can  establish but i think the most important  thing that he says is to just make time  for deep work so have a block of time  that is solely focused on deep work so  for me that's around four hours i would  say so i usually have this block in the  morning but what i noticed lately is  that i do have a little bit of trouble  on focusing in the morning so i want to  create two blocks or even three blocks  that i could have  for deep work so one is in the morning  one is in the afternoon and one is in  the evening and that's not to say that i  have to do every block  deep work but more to say that i have  three chances in a day to do  deep work and i want to catch one of  them because i notice in myself that  sometimes if i'm not productive in the  morning i really get into this mindset  of the day is lost it doesn't matter  anymore i can just spend the entire day  watching netflix because my morning has  been horrible  but i want to get out of this mindset  and try to  give myself three chances to do deep  work and just try to catch one of them  and i will focus for four hours and then  i think i should be able to manage some  deep work every day the second thing i  really wanted to focus on this week as  well is to create a little bit healthy  habits that i will force myself to do  during the lockdown because i remember  from last lockdown that i stopped  sleeping on time i stopped eating  healthy i ordered in all the time  because i felt so sad for myself and i  also completely stopped exercising so  this year i want to be my own strict mom  that tells me to wake up on time i will  try to  eat at least one healthy cooked meal a  day and then lastly  i will do  at least one hour of exercise outside if  possible  because  i know when the gyms are closing i get  really down just because i cannot move  and i think the gyms are closing  soon so i need to get this habit set  before  everything is going down and the world  is burning again  so yeah hopefully  i will manage that  and the last thing i also wanted to  focus on this week is to remind myself  that it's a marathon and not a sprint  and that's kind of to say that sometimes  when i have a really bad day or an off  day i can beat myself up about it  pretty bad i would say and i really just  want to let it go you know if i have a  bad day to just get over it and  keep on working so this week i also  really try to focus on that mindset  and  i'm not really sure how one can change  their mindset so that's why i'm just  saying it in the camera right now but i  think  i'm reminding myself here and there by  pulling little post-it notes it's a  marathon it's amazing it's a marathon  will remind myself that it's not that  bad if you sometimes  lose a day so yeah these were the three  things that i focused on and i hoped you  got some tips and tricks or at least  some inspiration of what to do  and if you are also struggling with  focus and you probably read a lot of  blogs and things as well  so if you have some tips or tricks for  me for the things you learned i would  love to hear them so put them down in  the comments below and otherwise see you  next week for another focus week  hopefully yes okay  see you bye

